857
00:27:52,384 --> 00:27:54,786
because that's an instant return on your

858
00:27:54,786 --> 00:27:55,146
money.

859
00:27:55,326 --> 00:27:58,273
Fourth, build your emergency fund to three

860
00:27:58,273 --> 00:28:00,098
to six months of expenses.

861
00:28:00,278 --> 00:28:03,109
Fifth, invest more for retirement,

862
00:28:03,109 --> 00:28:05,606
often in low cost index funds.

863
00:28:05,786 --> 00:28:08,243
And sixth, save for bigger goals like

864
00:28:08,243 --> 00:28:08,973
a car fund,

865
00:28:08,973 --> 00:28:11,429
a home, or your children's education.

866
00:28:11,778 --> 00:28:12,795
Follow that order,

867
00:28:12,795 --> 00:28:14,941
and every dollar you rescue from waste

868
00:28:14,941 --> 00:28:16,636
goes to work where it does the

869
00:28:16,636 --> 00:28:17,200
most good.

870
00:28:17,380 --> 00:28:19,383
The waste stops being invisible,

871
00:28:19,383 --> 00:28:22,137
and starts becoming your family's safety net

872
00:28:22,137 --> 00:28:22,825
and future.

873
00:28:23,175 --> 00:28:25,358
A few warnings before you start cutting.

874
00:28:25,538 --> 00:28:26,479
Mistake one.

875
00:28:26,659 --> 00:28:28,272
Cutting the wrong things.

876
00:28:28,452 --> 00:28:30,603
Some spending is an investment in your

877
00:28:30,603 --> 00:28:32,980
health, your relationships or your career.

878
00:28:33,160 --> 00:28:34,693
Don't skip the doctor,

879
00:28:34,693 --> 00:28:37,688
cancel the child's music lessons they love,

880
00:28:37,688 --> 00:28:40,196
or stop learning skills just to save

881
00:28:40,196 --> 00:28:41,171
a few dollars.

882
00:28:41,351 --> 00:28:43,185
Cut waste, not value.

883
00:28:43,535 --> 00:28:44,638
Mistake two.

884
00:28:44,818 --> 00:28:46,246
Cutting everything at once.

885
00:28:46,426 --> 00:28:48,679
Extreme budgets tend to snap back.

886
00:28:48,859 --> 00:28:51,018
Change one or two things a month,

887
00:28:51,018 --> 00:28:53,112
and let each new habit settle in

888
00:28:53,112 --> 00:28:54,617
before adding the next.

889
00:28:54,797 --> 00:28:55,900
Mistake three.

890
00:28:56,080 --> 00:28:58,275
Not giving the saved money a job.

891
00:28:58,455 --> 00:29:00,861
If you cancel a subscription but leave

892
00:29:00,861 --> 00:29:02,253
the money in checking,

893
00:29:02,253 --> 00:29:04,596
it usually gets spent somewhere else.

894
00:29:04,776 --> 00:29:07,221
Move it automatically to savings or debt

895
00:29:07,221 --> 00:29:08,015
the same day.

896
00:29:08,365 --> 00:29:09,561
And mistake four.

897
00:29:09,741 --> 00:29:12,377
Feeling guilty about past spending.

898
00:29:12,557 --> 00:29:14,182
Everyone has wasted money.

899
00:29:14,362 --> 00:29:16,283
The point isn't to punish yourself for

900
00:29:16,283 --> 00:29:16,789
yesterday.

901
00:29:16,969 --> 00:29:19,128
It's to make tomorrow's money work harder.

902
00:29:19,308 --> 00:29:20,568
Start where you are,

903
00:29:20,568 --> 00:29:21,764
with what you have,

904
00:29:21,764 --> 00:29:23,464
and let the progress build.

905
00:29:23,814 --> 00:29:24,616
Question one.

906
00:29:24,796 --> 00:29:27,232
Isn't the real problem that costs have

907
00:29:27,232 --> 00:29:27,744
gone up?

908
00:29:27,924 --> 00:29:29,478
Rising costs are real,

909
00:29:29,478 --> 00:29:32,301
and many families face genuine pressure.

910
00:29:32,481 --> 00:29:35,020
That's exactly why waste matters more now

911
00:29:35,020 --> 00:29:35,639
than ever.

912
00:29:35,819 --> 00:29:37,753
When every dollar is stretched,

913
00:29:37,753 --> 00:29:39,873
the dollars leaking into interest,

914
00:29:39,873 --> 00:29:42,367
fees and unused services hurt even more.

915
00:29:42,717 --> 00:29:43,565
Question two.

916
00:29:43,745 --> 00:29:45,150
Which one should I fix first?

917
00:29:45,330 --> 00:29:47,980
Start with high interest credit card debt,

918
00:29:47,980 --> 00:29:50,252
because it's expensive and it grows.

919
00:29:50,432 --> 00:29:52,264
Then look at your car and housing

920
00:29:52,264 --> 00:29:54,206
costs, because they're the biggest.

921
00:29:54,386 --> 00:29:56,336
The small stuff can come after.

922
00:29:56,686 --> 00:29:57,882
Question three.

923
00:29:58,062 --> 00:29:59,923
Do I need to give up vacations

924
00:29:59,923 --> 00:30:00,419
and fun?

925
00:30:00,599 --> 00:30:00,854
No.

926
00:30:01,034 --> 00:30:03,264
The goal isn't to stop enjoying life.

927
00:30:03,444 --> 00:30:05,113
It's to stop paying for things that

928
00:30:05,113 --> 00:30:06,114
don't make it better.

929
00:30:06,294 --> 00:30:07,422
Plan for fun,

930
00:30:07,422 --> 00:30:08,463
save for it,

931
00:30:08,463 --> 00:30:09,591
and pay cash.

932
00:30:09,771 --> 00:30:11,115
You'll enjoy it more,

933
00:30:11,115 --> 00:30:12,523
and it will cost less.

934
00:30:12,872 --> 00:30:13,790
Question four.

935
00:30:13,970 --> 00:30:16,744
My spouse and I disagree about spending.

936
00:30:16,924 --> 00:30:17,540
What now?

937
00:30:17,720 --> 00:30:19,963
Start by agreeing on shared goals,

938
00:30:19,963 --> 00:30:22,668
then give each person some personal money

939
00:30:22,668 --> 00:30:24,581
to spend without explanation.

940
00:30:24,761 --> 00:30:26,967
Many couples find that agreeing on the

941
00:30:26,967 --> 00:30:29,753
destination makes the daily choices much easier.

942
00:30:30,103 --> 00:30:31,172
Question five.

943
00:30:31,352 --> 00:30:33,073
Is it worth paying off my car

944
00:30:33,073 --> 00:30:33,430
early?

945
00:30:33,610 --> 00:30:35,407
If the interest rate is high,

946
00:30:35,407 --> 00:30:37,762
paying extra can be a great guaranteed

947
00:30:37,762 --> 00:30:38,196
return.

948
00:30:38,376 --> 00:30:40,004
If the rate is very low,

949
00:30:40,004 --> 00:30:42,921
many people prefer to build their emergency

950
00:30:42,921 --> 00:30:44,413
fund and invest first.

951
00:30:44,593 --> 00:30:46,841
Either way, the biggest win comes after

952
00:30:46,841 --> 00:30:47,648
the loan ends,

953
00:30:47,648 --> 00:30:49,377
when you keep the car and keep

954
00:30:49,377 --> 00:30:51,164
making the payment to yourself.

955
00:30:51,514 --> 00:30:52,536
Question six.

956
00:30:52,716 --> 00:30:54,266
How do I find my waste without

957
00:30:54,266 --> 00:30:55,352
tracking every penny?

958
00:30:55,532 --> 00:30:56,936
Look at three things.

959
00:30:57,116 --> 00:30:59,812
Your bank and card statements for anything

960
00:30:59,812 --> 00:31:01,352
that repeats each month,

961
00:31:01,352 --> 00:31:03,277
your biggest three categories,

962
00:31:03,277 --> 00:31:04,946
which are usually housing,

963
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:06,486
transportation and food,

964
00:31:06,486 --> 00:31:08,668
and any interest or fees you paid.

965
00:31:08,848 --> 00:31:10,733
Those three checks find most of the

966
00:31:10,733 --> 00:31:11,971
waste in about an hour.

967
00:31:12,321 --> 00:31:13,262
Question seven.

968
00:31:13,442 --> 00:31:15,706
Will cutting waste really make me wealthy?

969
00:31:15,886 --> 00:31:16,536
On its own,

970
00:31:16,536 --> 00:31:18,370
cutting waste creates the room.

971
00:31:18,550 --> 00:31:20,410
What makes you wealthy is what you

972
00:31:20,410 --> 00:31:21,395
do with that room.

973
00:31:21,575 --> 00:31:23,154
Pay off expensive debt,

974
00:31:23,154 --> 00:31:24,252
build a cushion,

975
00:31:24,252 --> 00:31:26,312
and invest steadily for years.

976
00:31:26,492 --> 00:31:28,442
Cutting waste is the first step.

977
00:31:28,622 --> 00:31:30,654
Investing the difference is the second.

978
00:31:31,003 --> 00:31:31,828
Quick recap.

979
00:31:32,008 --> 00:31:33,807
Angle one, the numbers.

980
00:31:33,987 --> 00:31:35,690
New cars on long loans,

981
00:31:35,690 --> 00:31:36,801
too much house,

982
00:31:36,801 --> 00:31:38,355
credit card interest,

983
00:31:38,355 --> 00:31:40,132
very expensive weddings,

984
00:31:40,132 --> 00:31:43,316
investment fees, wasted food and unused gym

985
00:31:43,316 --> 00:31:44,204
memberships.

986
00:31:44,554 --> 00:31:46,737
Angle two, the psychology.

987
00:31:46,917 --> 00:31:49,080
Keeping up with the neighbors,

988
00:31:49,080 --> 00:31:51,027
over the top kids' parties,

989
00:31:51,027 --> 00:31:52,469
vacations on credit,

990
00:31:52,469 --> 00:31:54,776
renovations that don't pay back,

991
00:31:54,776 --> 00:31:58,237
sports betting, gadget upgrades and brand names.

992
00:31:58,586 --> 00:32:00,305
Angle three, the playbook.

993
00:32:00,485 --> 00:32:01,970
A giant tax refund,

994
00:32:01,970 --> 00:32:03,925
never shopping insurance,

995
00:32:03,925 --> 00:32:05,488
the streaming stack,

996
00:32:05,488 --> 00:32:07,286
college without a plan,

997
00:32:07,286 --> 00:32:09,241
boats and toys on credit,

998
00:32:09,241 --> 00:32:11,352
and convenience by default.

999
00:32:11,701 --> 00:32:13,164
Here's what I want you to take

1000
00:32:13,164 --> 00:32:13,408
away.

1001
00:32:13,588 --> 00:32:15,238
The middle class is not doomed,

1002
00:32:15,238 --> 00:32:16,409
and you are not stuck.

1003
00:32:16,589 --> 00:32:17,664
Costs are high,

1004
00:32:17,664 --> 00:32:20,746
but inside almost every budget there's room

1005
00:32:20,746 --> 00:32:22,323
hiding in plain sight,

1006
00:32:22,323 --> 00:32:23,469
in car payments,

1007
00:32:23,469 --> 00:32:26,551
interest, fees and habits nobody questions.

1008
00:32:26,731 --> 00:32:28,210
Find it, give it a job,

1009
00:32:28,210 --> 00:32:29,238
and let it grow.

1010
00:32:29,418 --> 00:32:31,205
The middle class doesn't need to work

1011
00:32:31,205 --> 00:32:31,543
harder.

1012
00:32:31,723 --> 00:32:33,174
It needs to stop leaking.

1013
00:32:33,354 --> 00:32:35,255
Pick one item from each angle and

1014
00:32:35,255 --> 00:32:36,292
fix it this month.

1015
00:32:36,472 --> 00:32:37,880
If you want the full plan,

1016
00:32:37,880 --> 00:32:38,964
it's in my playbook,

1017
00:32:38,964 --> 00:32:40,373
linked in the description.

1018
00:32:40,553 --> 00:32:42,254
Tell me in the comments how much

1019
00:32:42,254 --> 00:32:43,583
you think you could save.

1020
00:32:43,763 --> 00:32:44,959
I'm Ryan Rover.

1021
00:32:45,139 --> 00:32:46,276
See you in the next one.
